# Ink and denim

An optional navy tee and denim composition with warm brown shoes, using the current g050 body and chin-length bob. It keeps the Brown hair setting without lavender tint. Both complete-look samples keep the tee/denim boundary and boots readable; Kitchen gives the outfit warmer, more shadowed light.

1. Open [Ink and denim in Wardrobe](http://127.0.0.1:5173/src/showcase.html?hairColour=%23413934&preset=casual&outfit=casual&style=ecru&frame=body&scene=studio&light=neutral&topColor=%2332495e&bottomColor=%2335485c&shoesColor=%2348382e) with the local review server running, or choose **Try Ink and denim** beneath the two starting looks. This opens the complete recipe in a fresh preview.
2. Wait for the look to finish loading. It restores **Studio → Neutral → Full look**. Choose **Save settings (JSON)** for a portable copy; the original [ink-denim.json](ink-denim.json) also remains available through **Open settings (JSON) ↑**.
3. Switch to **Portrait** to inspect the face, or choose **Kitchen** to inspect the room lighting. To return to the first lighting context, choose **Studio**, then **Neutral**.
4. In Portrait, choose **Resume motion** if paused, **Look with a smile**, then **Release**. This uses the existing viewing action; it is not stored in the settings.

| Context | Unchanged original |
| --- | --- |
| Neutral Studio, complete outfit | [Full look](../docs/evidence/nonhair-2026-10-03/ink-denim-look/archive/capture/neutral-body.png) |
| Neutral Studio, face | [Portrait](../docs/evidence/nonhair-2026-10-03/ink-denim-look/archive/capture/neutral-portrait.png) |
| Kitchen, complete outfit | [Full look](../docs/evidence/nonhair-2026-10-03/ink-denim-look/archive/capture/kitchen-body.png) |
| Kitchen, face | [Portrait](../docs/evidence/nonhair-2026-10-03/ink-denim-look/archive/capture/kitchen-portrait.png) |
| Existing small-smile action | [Held at 1.2 seconds](../docs/evidence/nonhair-2026-10-03/ink-denim-look/archive/capture/smile-held.png) |
| After manual Release | [0.5 seconds after release](../docs/evidence/nonhair-2026-10-03/ink-denim-look/archive/capture/smile-released.png) |

The file preserves the actual downloaded and reopened JSON bytes. Opening starts a fresh preview; camera orbit, clock and viewing action start fresh, so it does not promise identical images. Neutral is an inspection option, not colour calibration. The Brown hair setting reads ashier in Neutral and warmer in Kitchen; the darker hair edge is weaker against Kitchen's background.

The portraits still show coarse hair cards/stipple and jagged neckline edges. This is a supported clothing composition, not a finished character. These six contexts do not qualify other bodies, all angles, fit or continuous expression/movement. Release returns the action to idle; it does not restore the initial head pose. The captured smile change is subtle.

See the [original-image review and receipt](../docs/evidence/nonhair-2026-10-03/ink-denim-look/README.md) for the exact study, fixed sampling limits and independent critique.

[Compare the captured room, portrait and expression views](ink-denim-review.html) on one page, with the unchanged settings download and original-image links.
